---
// GDPR (EU 2016/679) privacy page. Filled for this site on 2026-10-26:
//   - Controller: Jo Fernwood. No postal address is published (BRIEF.md: the
//     service is online); contact is by email. If a postal address becomes
//     available, add it in section 1.
//   - No analytics (USE_ANALYTICS = false in src/config.ts): the starter's
//     Plausible paragraphs were deleted from section 3. Switching analytics on
//     later means restoring them from the Croftweaver starter
//     (new-website/templates/astro/src/pages/privacy.astro) and filling their slots.
//   - The "Do Not Track" paragraph in section 3 stays even without analytics
//     (California's CalOPPA). Base.astro reads a 'theme' key from local storage;
//     nothing on this site writes it. If you add a theme toggle that stores the
//     choice, say so in section 3.
//   - ANY third-party embed (YouTube iframe, remote Google Fonts) or analytics
//     tool needs this page re-checked BEFORE it ships.
//   - A solid baseline, not legal advice. When in doubt, have it reviewed.
// Keep one <h1>, the description in the 120-160 char window, no em dashes or
// banned contractions, and every email address behind <EmailLink>.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles personal data: no cookies, no analytics, Cloudflare Pages hosting, emails you send, and your rights under the GDPR.`}>
  <section class="wrap">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p>
      Last updated: 26 October 2026. This page explains which personal data this website
      processes, on what legal basis under the GDPR (EU 2016/679), and which
      rights you have.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <p>Responsible for data processing on this website:</p>
    <p>
      {CONTACT.person}, trading as {SITE.name}<br />
      Email: <EmailLink address={CONTACT.email} subject="Privacy request" /><br />
      Phone: <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref}>{CONTACT.phone}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>2. Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      This site is served by <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.,
      101 Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you visit a page,
      Cloudflare processes technical connection data (IP address, date and time,
      requested URL, referring page, browser user agent) to deliver the site, to
      protect it against attacks, and to give us traffic statistics (for example
      requests, visitors and their countries). The legal basis is our legitimate
      interest in operating a secure and fast website and in knowing how much it
      is used (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Cloudflare acts as our
      processor under Art. 28 GDPR; transfers to the USA are covered by the
      EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not
      combine these logs with any other data.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This website is ad-free and <strong>sets no cookies</strong>. Your visit
      leaves no advertising or cross-site tracking identifiers with us.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your browser may send a "Do Not Track" or "Global Privacy Control"
      signal. This site handles every visit the same way, with or without it:
      it does not follow you across other websites. The service providers named
      on this page process data for us as described here. No other third party
      collects personal information about you over time and across websites
      through this site.
    </p>
    <p>
      This site runs <strong>no analytics or tracking tool</strong>. No script
      measures your visit, and nothing is stored on or read from your device for
      that purpose. The only usage figures we can see are the traffic counts
      Cloudflare produces from its server logs, described in section 2.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact by email or phone</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact us by email or phone, we process the data you provide (name,
      email address or phone number, the content of your message, and any documents
      you send for a quote or translation) to handle the request and possible
      follow-up questions. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the request
      relates to a contract, otherwise our legitimate interest in answering
      enquiries (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). We keep the correspondence only as long as
      needed for this purpose and for any statutory retention duties.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you have the right of access (Art. 15), rectification
      (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), data
      portability (Art. 20), and objection to processing based on legitimate
      interest (Art. 21). To exercise any of these rights, contact us via the
      address in section 1; we will verify your identity before acting on a
      request. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data
      protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
    </p>

    <h2>6. Changes to this page</h2>
    <p>
      We will update this page whenever the data processing on this site
      changes, and adjust the date at the top accordingly.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
